{"name":"Derry Coast Sunrise","hex":"#f9e1cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"derry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A meaningless refrain or chorus."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Dislike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/derry"},{"term":"coast","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The edge of the land where it meets an ocean, sea, gulf, bay, or large lake. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The side or edge of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To glide along without adding energy; to allow a vehicle to continue moving forward after disengaging the engine or ceasing to apply motive power.","To sail along a coast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coast"},{"term":"sunrise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day when the sun appears above the eastern horizon.","The change in color of the sky at dawn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase in.","To awake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunrise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Derry","blocks":[{"text":"Derry, officially Londonderry, is a cathedral city in Northern Ireland. Located in County Londonderry, the city now covers both banks of the River Foyle. Cityside and the old walled city are on the west bank and Waterside is on the east, with two road bridges and one footbridge crossing the river in between."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Foyle_Bridge_Derry_at_Dusk_Oblique.jpg/330px-Foyle_Bridge_Derry_at_Dusk_Oblique.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derry","wikidata":"Q163584"},{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast","wikidata":"Q93352"},{"title":"Sunrise","blocks":[{"text":"Sunrise is the moment when the upper rim of the Sun appears on the horizon in the morning, at the start of the Sun path. The term can also refer to the entire process of the solar disk crossing the horizon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunrise","wikidata":"Q193294"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Derry_Guildhall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7092729.jpg/500px-Derry_Guildhall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7092729.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Derry_Guildhall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7092729.jpg/500px-Derry_Guildhall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7092729.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADerry_Guildhall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7092729.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/%22Hands_Across_the_Divide%22_sculpture%2C_Derry_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-%22Hands_Across_the_Divide%22_sculpture%2C_Derry_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/%22Hands_Across_the_Divide%22_sculpture%2C_Derry_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-%22Han